/*
Time Complexity: O(n · 2^n) There are O(2^n) possible partitions in the worst case, and each palindrome check costs O(n).
Space Complexity: O(n) auxiliary space + O(2^n) output space
1️⃣ Recursion stack

Maximum depth occurs when every character is its own substring.

Depth = O(n)

2️⃣ Current partition storage

At most n substrings in cur.

3️⃣ Output storage

Stores all valid partitions → exponential.



INTUITION
We try to cut the string into pieces such that every piece is a palindrome.

start marks where the current substring begins.

end keeps expanding to form the current substring s[start…end].

If s[start…end] is a palindrome:

Add it to the current partition.

Start a new substring from end + 1.

Whether palindrome or not, we also try to extend end to include more characters.

When end reaches the end of the string:

If start == end, it means the whole string has been validly partitioned.

Add the current partition to the result.

Backtrack by removing the last added substring and try other possibilities.

*/
class Solution {
    List<List<String>> res = new ArrayList<>();
    List<String> cur = new ArrayList<>();
    public List<List<String>> partition(String s) {
        dfs(0,0,s);
        return res;
    }
    public void dfs(int start,int end,String s){
        if(end>=s.length()){
            if(start==end){
                //end has already travelled entire string from start
                // if start is already equal to end then we've got last valid palindrome in this path
                // add to res
                res.add(new ArrayList<>(cur));
            }
            return;
        }
        if(isPalindrome(s,start,end)){
            cur.add(s.substring(start,end+1));
            // we already got a palindrome , start new string from next index
            dfs(end+1,end+1,s);
            cur.remove(cur.size()-1);
        }
        //add next character to current string
        dfs(start,end+1,s);
    }
    public boolean isPalindrome(String s , int l ,int r){
        while(l<r){
            if(s.charAt(l)!=s.charAt(r))return false;
            l++;
            r--;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
